<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Yemen Arab Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1962 CE – 1990 CE · capital Sanaa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">North Yemen's republic, born in the 1962 revolution against the imamate, which fought a long civil war before uniting with the South in 1990.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 26 September 1962 army officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-al-sallal">Abdullah al-Sallal</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-badr">Muhammad al-Badr</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mutawakkilite-kingdom-of-yemen">Mutawakkilite Kingdom of Yemen</a> and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> Arab Republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> sent tens of thousands of troops to defend it, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a> backed the royalists.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The civil war lasted until 1970, when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a> recognised the republic. Politics remained dominated by army officers and tribal leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hashid">Hashid</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakil">Bakil</a> confederations. President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-al-hamdi">Ibrahim al-Hamdi</a> was assassinated in 1977, and his successor too, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Ali Abdullah Saleh</a> took power in 1978. Remittances from workers in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> sustained the economy, and oil was found near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a> in 1984.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After border wars in 1972 and 1979 and years of talks, North <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> united with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> on 22 May 1990 to form the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Saleh</a> as president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/yemen-arab-republic.jpg" alt="Yemen Arab Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: B1mbo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Yemen_Arab_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1962 CE – 1990 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sanaa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah al-Sallal, Ibrahim al-Hamdi, Ali Abdullah Saleh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam (Zaydi and Sunni)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>North Yemen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1976&amp;focus=yemen-arab-republic" aria-label="Yemen Arab Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5887 1607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Yemen Arab Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6207 1863L6206 1928M6207 1863L6207 1863"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6206 1928h0M6207 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6207 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6207 1863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sanaa. <a href="/atlas?year=1976&amp;focus=yemen-arab-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
